& [ConstraintClassification] is explicit
  + [hard] must hold for CTPR canonical authority
  + [profile] must hold when a temporal, repository, lane, compiler, or provider profile selects behavior
  + [implementation] requires later code and deterministic proof
  + [runtime] is revalidated for every live use
  + [experimental] is a candidate whose benefit and semantic correspondence remain unproved

& [ConstraintSet_IdentityAndAuthority] is checked
  + [C01_source_preservation] hard: raw CTPR source remains immutable and content-bound
    @ [status] satisfied
  + [C02_SMTC_dependency] hard: CTPR compiler semantics consume valid bounded SMTC-SJS-01 without inheriting implementation authority
    @ [status] satisfied
  + [C03_Planner_proposal] hard: Planner projects candidate paths and cannot make facts, commitments, or effect grants
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C04_Calendar_projection] hard: Calendar records local temporal proposals and commitments separately from provider synchronization
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C05_Observer_admission] hard: only an eligible ObserverJoin admits a successor repository generation
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C06_effect_separation] hard: calendar sync, notification, Git write, file write, provider call, background work, and external mutation require separate authority
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C07_signature_noninheritance] hard: external Walking Attention behavior does not transfer external signature authority
    @ [status] satisfied

& [ConstraintSet_TimeAndCalendar] is checked
  + [C08_time_domains] hard: civil, instant, monotonic, logical, valid, transaction, and uncertain time remain distinct
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C09_time_evidence] hard: asserted time binds source, zone where applicable, precision, interpretation, and uncertainty
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C10_no_timestamp_causality] hard: timestamps, record position, operand order, or digest do not prove causal order alone
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C11_schedule_commitment] hard: schedule candidate, accepted commitment, provider synchronization, trigger, and completion are separate states
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C12_wake_revalidation] runtime: wake checks current assumptions, dependencies, authority, targets, relevance, privacy, and effect scope before work
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented
  + [C13_recurrence_bounds] profile: expansion has zone policy, exceptions, finite horizon, and occurrence identity
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented

& [ConstraintSet_RepositoryAndHistory] is checked
  + [C14_material_capture] hard: every materially observable transition is recorded; insignificant events are not required by default
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C15_no_moment_flood] hard: every moment is interpreted through explicit materiality and retention policy
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C16_append_only_history] hard: prior source, plan, intent, event, diff, review, and disposition remain immutable
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C17_no_atomic_overclaim] hard: sequential observations and semantic snapshots do not claim atomic external-world state
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C18_Git_projection] hard: Git is a human-facing milestone projection, not the sole semantic repository
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C19_unrelated_attribution] hard: unrelated dirty or external state is preserved separately from claimed work
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C20_compaction_equivalence] implementation: aggregation, compaction, redaction, or deletion declares loss, proof impact, and replay boundary
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented

& [ConstraintSet_ChangeAndReflection] is checked
  + [C21_ChangeCapsule_waist] hard: declared intent, before state, candidate, observed result, diffs, review, disposition, and after state remain joined by one stable capsule identity
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C22_distinct_diff_surfaces] hard: physical, source, semantic, build, behavioral, effect, proof, and calendar changes are not collapsed
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C23_rear_refusal] hard: rear review may report no change, mismatch, repair, blockage, or unresolved state and can refuse completion
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C24_no_hindsight_rewrite] hard: review-derived requirements and lessons do not alter prior declared intent or forecast
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C25_evidence_backed_review] hard: files, commits, source, events, tests, and proof artifacts support review; private reasoning does not
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade

& [ConstraintSet_LanesAndConcurrency] is checked
  + [C26_immutable_lane_inputs] hard: every lane reads exact immutable versions
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C27_no_shared_mutable_attention] hard: lanes exchange versioned messages and do not mutate one live semantic or hidden attention state
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C28_prepared_not_admitted] hard: prepared-ahead work cannot commit dependent effects or successor state
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C29_compare_and_append] implementation: joins reject stale predecessors, generations, dependencies, and authorities
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented
  + [C30_bounded_lag] profile: any reflection lag names eligibility, count or duration, consequence, rollback, overdue behavior, and authority
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented
  + [C31_no_deadlock] implementation: timeout, cancellation, residual, crash reentry, and terminal disposition prevent indefinite review blocking
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented

& [ConstraintSet_CompilerLearningAndProjection] is checked
  + [C32_bidirectional_compiler] hard: forward parse, resolve, lower, and project remain distinct from rear source, semantic, impact, correspondence, and proof review
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C33_independent_correspondence] hard: generated target output cannot be its only correctness evidence
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C34_invalidation_graph] implementation: semantic changes propagate to affected IR, indexes, packages, schedules, workflows, models, tools, and hardware projections
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented
  + [C35_lesson_candidate] hard: forecast error, deviation, and surprise remain reviewed candidates before SOP, policy, or corpus adoption
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C36_deterministic_fallback] hard: exact local planning, repository, replay, and refusal remain valid without model or provider
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C37_ECS_projection_only] experimental: ECS may optimize runtime shape but cannot replace semantic identity, contextual graph relations, provenance, truth status, authority, or proof
    @ [status] considered_not_selected
  + [C38_first_fixture_only] hard: the next possible implementation scope is one deterministic fake calendar, repository, tandem, and compiler-diff fixture
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade

& [ConstraintSet_PrivacyRetentionAndScope] is checked
  + [C39_field_sensitivity] hard: calendar, source, diff, prompt, provider, tool, trace, proof, and lesson fields have independent sensitivity and disclosure
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C40_retention_rights] profile: transient, durable, archived, compacted, redacted, and deleted states bind policy and proof impact
    @ [status] formed_not_implemented
  + [C41_index_nonleakage] hard: index or embedding access cannot disclose protected source or relations beyond query authority
    @ [status] satisfied_at_specification_grade
  + [C42_no_live_authority] hard: current signature grants no live clock, provider, calendar, notification, background journal, Git mutation, concurrent agent, model training, FPGA, desktop, or external effect
    @ [status] satisfied_by_planned_scope

& [CollisionReview] resolves candidate tensions
  + [collision_1] Planner_central versus Planner_not_authority resolves through candidate projection and Observer selection
  + [collision_2] Calendar_central versus no_provider_access resolves through local temporal representation before optional effect adapters
  + [collision_3] every_moment versus finite_storage resolves through materiality, aggregation, retention, and explicit loss
  + [collision_4] snapshot_repository versus no_atomic_world_claim resolves through semantic frontier snapshots of sequential admitted observations
  + [collision_5] simultaneous_attention versus no_shared_state resolves through prepared-ahead versioned lanes and message joins
  + [collision_6] rear_reflection_changes_work versus history_immutability resolves through invalidation and new plan generations
  + [collision_7] compiler_self_review versus independent_proof resolves through distinct rear analyzers and independent evidence
  + [collision_8] learned_lessons versus no_hindsight resolves through preserved source plus separately reviewed LessonCandidate
  + [collision_9] Walking_Attention_import versus unsigned_controller resolves through cited behavior and CTPR-owned derived semantics without signature inheritance
  + [collision_10] ECS_efficiency versus semantic_graph_richness resolves through optional projection and graph-preserving correspondence

& [ConstraintDisposition] is phase-lock eligible
  + [constraint_count] is 42
  + [hard_failure_count] is 0
  + [profile_deferred_count] is 4
  + [implementation_or_runtime_deferred_count] is 7
  + [experimental_candidate_count] is 1
  + [deferred_authority] is none
  + [source_revision_required] is false
  + [canonical_scope] is CTPR semantic and logical authority with deterministic-fixture-only future frontier and no current implementation

& [Invalidation] is fail-closed
  + any hard constraint failure
  + source or upstream SMTC drift
  + external selected Walking Attention evidence drift without recheck
  + hidden-state, shared-mutation, history-rewrite, false-atomicity, provider, effect, privacy, compiler-self-proof, or signature-inheritance expansion
  + treating deferred implementation or experimental ECS as completed proof
